{
  "id": "neonatal-glucose-management-dt",
  "title": "32–35 wk Neonate Born",
  "subtitle": "All 32–35 wk neonates are at-risk for hypoglycemia",
  "version": "1.0",
  "source": "",
  "mode": "neonatal",
  "root": {
    "id": "neonatal_glucose_management_dt-32-35-wk-neonate-born-1",
    "label": "32–35 wk Neonate Born",
    "type": "assessment",
    "description": "All 32–35 wk neonates are at-risk for hypoglycemia",
    "panels": [
      {
        "label": "Risk Factors",
        "type": "html",
        "content": {
          "html": "<p><strong>ALL neonates 32 0/7 – 35 6/7 weeks</strong> are inherently at-risk due to limited glycogen stores, immature counter-regulatory hormones, and high brain-to-body glucose demand.</p>\n<table class=\"rt\"><thead><tr><th>Risk Factor</th><th>Evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td>SGA (&lt;10th %ile)</td><td>19.4% incidence; 53% of DOL2 cases</td></tr>\n<tr><td>LGA (&gt;90th %ile)</td><td>Significant early severe hypoglycemia risk</td></tr>\n<tr><td>IDM (insulin-treated GDM)</td><td>Independent on multivariate analysis</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Maternal Hypertensive Disorders</td><td>OR 2.1 for hypoglycemia admission</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Antenatal Betamethasone</td><td>82% maternal hyperglycemia; ↑ neonatal risk</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Cesarean Delivery</td><td>Independent risk in SGA neonates</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Hypothermia</td><td>aOR 2.10 for NICU transfer</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Low 1-min Apgar (&lt;7)</td><td>Significant in SGA neonates</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>"
        }
      },
      {
        "label": "Immediate Care",
        "type": "html",
        "content": {
          "html": "<p><strong>First 30 minutes:</strong></p><ul class=\"sl\"><li>Skin-to-skin contact immediately</li><li>Thermoregulation (target axillary 36.5–37.5°C)</li><li>Encourage breastfeeding within 30–60 min</li><li>Assess: jitteriness, poor feeding, lethargy, apnea, seizures</li></ul>\n<p><strong>First glucose:</strong> Within 1 hour of birth. Use validated POC device. Confirm &lt;25 mg/dL with lab glucose if available within 30 min — do NOT delay treatment.</p>"
        }
      },
      {
        "label": "Evidence",
        "type": "html",
        "content": {
          "html": "<div class=\"bx bb\">ℹ️ <strong>AAP (Adamkin 2011):</strong> No specific glucose concentration reliably discriminates normal from abnormal. Early identification + prophylactic measures recommended.<br><span style=\"font-size:10px;opacity:.7\">DOI: 10.1542/peds.2010-3851</span></div>\n<div class=\"bx bb\">ℹ️ <strong>Narasimhan et al. 2021:</strong> 84 US hospitals showed wide variation in definitions (&lt;25 to &lt;45), timing (30 min to 2 hr), and transfer criteria.<br><span style=\"font-size:10px;opacity:.7\">DOI: 10.1542/hpeds.2020-004101</span></div>\n<div class=\"bx bb\">ℹ️ <strong>Cochrane (Edwards 2022):</strong> 40% dextrose gel ↑ correction (RR 1.08), ↓ separation (RR 0.54), ↑ breastfeeding (RR 1.10). No adverse events.<br><span style=\"font-size:10px;opacity:.7\">DOI: 10.1002/14651858.CD011027.pub3</span></div>"
        }
      },
      {
        "label": "Alerts",
        "type": "html",
        "content": {
          "html": "<div class=\"bx br\">🚨 <strong>Hypothermia–Hypoglycemia Link:</strong> Hypothermia accelerates glycogen depletion via non-shivering thermogenesis. Aggressive thermoregulation = prevention. (Kurz 2025, DOI: 10.1186/s40348-025-00204-1)</div>\n<div class=\"bx br\">🚨 <strong>Rural Setting:</strong> Establish transfer criteria BEFORE decompensation. Know transport times + NICU bed availability. Dextrose gel can eliminate transfers at Level 1 facilities (Deyo-Svendsen 2021, PMID: 33974766).</div>"
        }
      }
    ],
    "children": [
      {
        "label": "Screen\nall",
        "node": {
          "id": "neonatal_glucose_management_dt-first-glucose-check-1-hr-2",
          "label": "First Glucose Check ≤1 hr",
          "type": "action",
          "description": "POC glucose before first feed",
          "panels": [
            {
              "label": "Screening Protocol",
              "type": "html",
              "content": {
                "html": "<table class=\"rt\"><thead><tr><th>Period</th><th>Frequency</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td>0–4 hours</td><td>Every 1 hour (before each feed)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4–24 hours</td><td>Pre-feed (Q2–3 hr)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>24–48 hours</td><td>Pre-feed if borderline; d/c if ≥50 × 3</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>"
              }
            },
            {
              "label": "Timing Evidence",
              "type": "html",
              "content": {
                "html": "<div class=\"bx bb\">ℹ️ <strong>Wang et al. 2023:</strong> 97% of hypoglycemic episodes in SGA neonates within first 2 hours. Lowest glucose at 1 hour.<br><span style=\"font-size:10px;opacity:.7\">DOI: 10.1016/j.pedneo.2022.09.021</span></div>\n<div class=\"bx bb\">ℹ️ <strong>El-Khawam 2024:</strong> 3.1% of at-risk neonates had glucose ≤25 in first hour; 0.5% had ≤10 mg/dL.<br><span style=\"font-size:10px;opacity:.7\">DOI: 10.1515/jpem-2023-0573</span></div>"
              }
            },
            {
              "label": "Measurement",
              "type": "html",
              "content": {
                "html": "<p>Use validated bedside glucose analyzer. Adult meters may be unreliable at low neonatal concentrations. Confirm critical value (&lt;25) with lab — do NOT delay treatment.</p>"
              }
            }
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "label": "Symptomatic",
              "node": {
                "id": "neonatal_glucose_management_dt-symptomatic-any-glucose-45-3",
                "label": "SYMPTOMATIC Any Glucose <45",
                "type": "emergency",
                "description": "Seizures, apnea, lethargy, poor feeding",
                "panels": [
                  {
                    "label": "Emergency Protocol",
                    "type": "html",
                    "content": {
                      "html": "<div class=\"bx br\">🚨 <strong>SYMPTOMATIC HYPOGLYCEMIA = EMERGENCY</strong></div>\n<ul class=\"sl\"><li>D10W IV bolus: 2 mL/kg over 5–10 min</li><li>Start continuous D10W at GIR 5–8 mg/kg/min</li><li>Recheck glucose 15–30 min post-bolus</li><li>Titrate GIR to maintain ≥50 mg/dL</li><li>Do NOT use gel alone for symptomatic hypoglycemia</li></ul>"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "label": "IV Dosing",
                    "type": "html",
                    "content": {
                      "html": "<table class=\"rt\"><thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Value</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td>Bolus</td><td>D10W 2 mL/kg IV over 5–10 min</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Initial GIR</td><td>5–8 mg/kg/min</td></tr>\n<tr><td>GIR Formula</td><td>(Dex% × Rate mL/hr) / (6 × Wt kg)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>D10W @ 80 mL/kg/day</td><td>GIR ≈ 5.6 mg/kg/min</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Target</td><td>≥50 mg/dL</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Monitor</td><td>Q30 min → Q1–2 hr once stable</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<div class=\"bx br\">🚨 NEVER use D25W or D50W in neonates (osmotic injury + rebound hypoglycemia)</div>"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "label": "Escalation",
                    "type": "html",
                    "content": {
                      "html": "<p><strong>GIR &gt;10–12 → Hyperinsulinism workup:</strong></p>\n<table class=\"rt\"><thead><tr><th>Lab</th><th>Significance</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td>Insulin</td><td>Detectable during hypo = hyperinsulinism</td></tr>\n<tr><td>C-peptide</td><td>Elevated: endogenous production</td></tr>\n<tr><td>FFA</td><td>Suppressed: hyperinsulinism</td></tr>\n<tr><td>BHB</td><td>Suppressed: no ketone generation</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Cortisol / GH</td><td>Low: adrenal/GH deficiency</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Ammonia, Lactate</td><td>Metabolic disease screen</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<div class=\"bx bb\">ℹ️ <strong>Al Housni 2022:</strong> Medication cohort max GIR 12.95 vs 6.77 mg/kg/min. Predictors: GDM, LGA, BG ≤1.5 mmol/L at 2hr.<br><span style=\"font-size:10px;opacity:.7\">DOI: 10.7759/cureus.32197</span></div>"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "label": "Transfer",
                    "type": "html",
                    "content": {
                      "html": "<div class=\"bx br\">🚨 <strong>Transfer to Level III/IV when:</strong><ul><li>Seizures</li><li>Persistent symptomatic hypoglycemia</li><li>GIR &gt;12 mg/kg/min</li><li>Suspected hyperinsulinism</li><li>Unable to wean IV after 3–5 days</li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"bx bg\">✅ <strong>Continue Level II when:</strong><ul><li>Responding to gel + feeds</li><li>GIR &lt;10 with stable values</li><li>Asymptomatic throughout</li><li>Enteral feeds advancing, IV weaning within 24–48 hr</li></ul></div>"
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "children": [
                  {
                    "label": "IV\naccess",
                    "node": {
                      "id": "neonatal_glucose_management_dt-iv-d10w-bolus-2-ml-kg-gir-5-8-4",
                      "label": "IV D10W Bolus 2 mL/kg + GIR 5–8",
                      "type": "emergency",
                      "description": "Recheck 15–30 min post-bolus",
                      "panels": [
                        {
                          "label": "Protocol",
                          "type": "html",
                          "content": {
                            "html": "<ul class=\"sl\"><li>D10W 2 mL/kg IV push over 5–10 min</li><li>Start continuous infusion immediately</li><li>Recheck glucose 15–30 min post-bolus</li><li>Titrate up 1–2 mg/kg/min if glucose remains low</li></ul>"
                          }
                        }
                      ],
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "label": "Stable",
                          "node": {
                            "id": "neonatal_glucose_management_dt-stable-50-wean-gir-10-20-q6-12h-5",
                            "label": "Stable ≥50 → Wean GIR 10–20% Q6–12h",
                            "type": "action",
                            "description": "Advance enteral feeds; d/c IV when GIR <3",
                            "panels": [
                              {
                                "label": "Weaning",
                                "type": "html",
                                "content": {
                                  "html": "<p>Once ≥50 for ≥12 hr, wean GIR by 1–2 mg/kg/min (10–20%) every 6–12 hr. Check before each reduction. Advance enteral feeds. D/C IV when stable on full feeds with GIR &lt;3.</p>"
                                }
                              }
                            ]
                          }
                        },
                        {
                          "label": "Not\nresponding",
                          "node": {
                            "id": "neonatal_glucose_management_dt-gir-12-hyperinsulinism-workup-transfer-6",
                            "label": "GIR >12 → Hyperinsulinism Workup + Transfer",
                            "type": "diagnosis",
                            "description": "Critical sample during hypoglycemia",
                            "panels": [
                              {
                                "label": "Workup",
                                "type": "html",
                                "content": {
                                  "html": "<p>Obtain critical sample during hypoglycemia. Start diazoxide 5–15 mg/kg/day if confirmed hyperinsulinism. Transfer to Level III/IV with endocrine access.</p>"
                                }
                              }
                            ]
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "label": "Asymp\n<25",
              "node": {
                "id": "neonatal_glucose_management_dt-asymptomatic-glucose-25-0-4-hr-7",
                "label": "ASYMPTOMATIC Glucose <25 (0–4 hr)",
                "type": "urgent",
                "description": "Immediate dextrose gel + feed",
                "panels": [
                  {
                    "label": "Management",
                    "type": "html",
                    "content": {
                      "html": "<ul class=\"sl\"><li>40% dextrose gel 200 mg/kg buccally</li><li>Feed immediately — breast milk preferred</li><li>Recheck 30 min post-intervention</li><li>If &lt;25 after 2nd gel dose → IV D10W GIR 5–6</li></ul>"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "label": "Gel Dosing",
                    "type": "html",
                    "content": {
                      "html": "<table class=\"rt\"><thead><tr><th>Weight</th><th>Volume 40% Gel</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td>1.5 kg</td><td>0.75 mL</td></tr>\n<tr><td>2.0 kg</td><td>1.0 mL</td></tr>\n<tr><td>2.5 kg</td><td>1.25 mL</td></tr>\n<tr><td>3.0 kg</td><td>1.5 mL</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Dry buccal mucosa with gauze → apply gel to inner cheek → massage 1 min → feed immediately.</p>"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "label": "Evidence",
                    "type": "html",
                    "content": {
                      "html": "<div class=\"bx bb\">ℹ️ <strong>Cochrane (Edwards 2022):</strong> 40% gel probably ↑ correction, ↓ separation (RR 0.54), ↑ breastfeeding (RR 1.10). No adverse events. First-line for at-risk late preterm/term infants.<br><span style=\"font-size:10px;opacity:.7\">DOI: 10.1002/14651858.CD011027.pub3</span></div>\n<div class=\"bx bb\">ℹ️ <strong>Makker 2018:</strong> NICU transfers 8.1% → 3.7%; breastfeeding 6% → 19%; charges halved.<br><span style=\"font-size:10px;opacity:.7\">DOI: 10.1055/s-0038-1639338</span></div>\n<div class=\"bx bg\">✅ <strong>St Clair 2021:</strong> Dextrose gel does NOT alter neonatal gut microbiome.<br><span style=\"font-size:10px;opacity:.7\">DOI: 10.1136/archdischild-2021-322757</span></div>"
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "children": [
                  {
                    "label": "Gel +\nfeed",
                    "node": {
                      "id": "neonatal_glucose_management_dt-gel-200-mg-kg-feed-8",
                      "label": "Gel 200 mg/kg + Feed",
                      "type": "action",
                      "description": "Recheck 30 min",
                      "panels": [
                        {
                          "label": "Technique",
                          "type": "html",
                          "content": {
                            "html": "<ul class=\"sl\"><li>Draw 0.5 mL/kg of 40% dextrose gel</li><li>Dry buccal mucosa with gauze</li><li>Apply to inner cheek</li><li>Massage 1 minute</li><li>Follow with breastfeeding or EBM</li><li>Recheck glucose 30 min later</li></ul>"
                          }
                        }
                      ],
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "label": "≥25",
                          "node": {
                            "id": "neonatal_glucose_management_dt-recheck-25-continue-q1hr-screening-9",
                            "label": "Recheck ≥25 → Continue Q1hr Screening",
                            "type": "action",
                            "description": "Target rising trajectory → ≥45 by 4 hr",
                            "panels": [
                              {
                                "label": "Next",
                                "type": "html",
                                "content": {
                                  "html": "<p>Continue pre-feed screening Q1hr for first 4 hours. Target: rising trajectory toward ≥45 by 4 hr. Gel + feed for subsequent lows.</p>"
                                }
                              }
                            ]
                          }
                        },
                        {
                          "label": "Still\n<25",
                          "node": {
                            "id": "neonatal_glucose_management_dt-still-25-after-2-doses-iv-d10w-10",
                            "label": "Still <25 After 2 Doses → IV D10W",
                            "type": "urgent",
                            "description": "Failure of first-line therapy",
                            "panels": [
                              {
                                "label": "Escalation",
                                "type": "html",
                                "content": {
                                  "html": "<p>Failure of 2 gel doses → IV D10W at GIR 5–6 mg/kg/min. Do not delay further. Continue enteral feeds alongside IV.</p>"
                                }
                              }
                            ]
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "label": "Asymp\n25–39",
              "node": {
                "id": "neonatal_glucose_management_dt-asymptomatic-25-39-mg-dl-0-4-hr-11",
                "label": "ASYMPTOMATIC 25–39 mg/dL (0–4 hr)",
                "type": "decision",
                "description": "Feed ± dextrose gel",
                "panels": [
                  {
                    "label": "Management",
                    "type": "html",
                    "content": {
                      "html": "<ul class=\"sl\"><li>Feed immediately (breast milk preferred)</li><li>Consider adjunctive 40% gel 200 mg/kg</li><li>Recheck 30 min post-feed</li><li>&lt;25 → IV dextrose</li><li>25–39 not rising × 2 → consider IV</li><li>≥40 → continue screening</li></ul>"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "label": "Rural Evidence",
                    "type": "html",
                    "content": {
                      "html": "<div class=\"bx bg\">✅ <strong>Deyo-Svendsen 2021 (Level 1 Rural):</strong> Protocolized screening + gel eliminated ALL IV dextrose use and NICU transfers (0/250 vs 7/310 pre-protocol).<br><span style=\"font-size:10px;opacity:.7\">PMID: 33974766</span></div>\n<div class=\"bx bb\">ℹ️ <strong>Hammer 2018:</strong> Level 2 nursery toolkit → 6.5% ↑ exclusive breastfeeding, 5% ↓ intermediate care admissions.<br><span style=\"font-size:10px;opacity:.7\">DOI: 10.1097/ANC.0000000000000527</span></div>"
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "children": [
                  {
                    "label": "Feed ±\ngel",
                    "node": {
                      "id": "neonatal_glucose_management_dt-feed-gel-recheck-30-min-12",
                      "label": "Feed + Gel → Recheck 30 min",
                      "type": "action",
                      "description": "Goal: rising trajectory",
                      "panels": [
                        {
                          "label": "Protocol",
                          "type": "html",
                          "content": {
                            "html": "<p>Feed first, then gel if available. Recheck 30 min. If ≥40 → pre-feed monitoring Q1–2hr.</p>"
                          }
                        }
                      ],
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "label": "Rising",
                          "node": {
                            "id": "neonatal_glucose_management_dt-rising-pre-feed-screening-13",
                            "label": "Rising → Pre-feed Screening",
                            "type": "action",
                            "description": "Target ≥45 by 4–12 hr, ≥50 by 24 hr",
                            "panels": [
                              {
                                "label": "Targets",
                                "type": "html",
                                "content": {
                                  "html": "<table class=\"rt\"><thead><tr><th>Age</th><th>Target</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>0–4 hr</td><td>≥25 (some: ≥40)</td></tr><tr><td>4–24 hr</td><td>≥35–45</td></tr><tr><td>24–48 hr</td><td>≥50 (PES)</td></tr></tbody></table><p>May d/c screening after 3 consecutive ≥50 on full feeds.</p>"
                                }
                              }
                            ]
                          }
                        },
                        {
                          "label": "Not\nrising",
                          "node": {
                            "id": "neonatal_glucose_management_dt-not-rising-2-iv-d10w-14",
                            "label": "Not Rising × 2 → IV D10W",
                            "type": "urgent",
                            "description": "First-line failure after ~1 hr",
                            "panels": [
                              {
                                "label": "Escalation",
                                "type": "html",
                                "content": {
                                  "html": "<p>If not rising above 25 or no upward trend after 2 cycles (~1 hour), start IV D10W at GIR 5–6 mg/kg/min.</p>"
                                }
                              }
                            ]
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "label": "Asymp\n≥40",
              "node": {
                "id": "neonatal_glucose_management_dt-asymptomatic-40-mg-dl-0-4-hr-15",
                "label": "ASYMPTOMATIC ≥40 mg/dL (0–4 hr)",
                "type": "assessment",
                "description": "Continue monitoring",
                "panels": [
                  {
                    "label": "Monitoring",
                    "type": "html",
                    "content": {
                      "html": "<table class=\"rt\"><thead><tr><th>Age</th><th>Target</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td>0–4 hr</td><td>≥25 (some: ≥40)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4–24 hr</td><td>≥35–45</td></tr>\n<tr><td>24–48 hr</td><td>≥50 (PES threshold)</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "label": "Discharge",
                    "type": "html",
                    "content": {
                      "html": "<p><strong>D/C screening when:</strong></p><ul><li>3 consecutive pre-feed ≥50 mg/dL</li><li>Feeding well (breast or bottle)</li><li>Normothermic</li><li>Asymptomatic</li><li>≥24–48 hours old</li></ul>"
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "children": [
                  {
                    "label": "Monitor",
                    "node": {
                      "id": "neonatal_glucose_management_dt-pre-feed-q2-3hr-through-24-hr-16",
                      "label": "Pre-feed Q2–3hr Through 24 hr",
                      "type": "action",
                      "description": "If any value drops → re-enter branch",
                      "panels": [
                        {
                          "label": "Protocol",
                          "type": "html",
                          "content": {
                            "html": "<p>Continue pre-feed screening. If any value drops below threshold, re-enter appropriate branch. Support breastfeeding. Maintain thermoregulation.</p>"
                          }
                        }
                      ],
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "label": "Stable",
                          "node": {
                            "id": "neonatal_glucose_management_dt-3-50-d-c-screening-17",
                            "label": "3× ≥50 → D/C Screening",
                            "type": "action",
                            "description": "Screening complete",
                            "panels": [
                              {
                                "label": "Done",
                                "type": "html",
                                "content": {
                                  "html": "<p>Screening complete. Ensure feeding adequacy, temperature stability, normal assessment before discharge.</p>"
                                }
                              }
                            ]
                          }
                        },
                        {
                          "label": "Drop",
                          "node": {
                            "id": "neonatal_glucose_management_dt-value-drops-re-enter-branch-18",
                            "label": "Value Drops → Re-enter Branch",
                            "type": "decision",
                            "description": "Single recurrence: gel. Persistent: IV.",
                            "panels": [
                              {
                                "label": "Re-assess",
                                "type": "html",
                                "content": {
                                  "html": "<p>Any drop below threshold → re-enter at appropriate branch. Single recurrence: gel + feed. Persistent recurrence: IV dextrose.</p>"
                                }
                              }
                            ]
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
